 rec 169 zn_uptake_kinetic_basis = 1 : the ZINC active term is now a SATURATING FUNCTION OF THE ROOT-SURFACE CONCENTRATION, S_hats = mm_field_rate(Zn) x MAX(0,W_root) x a_root x c_surf / (km_zn_mgL + c_surf), with c_surf = soln - S_diff / (RLD_e x De_e x mm_depth_m x 86400 x 1e3), i.e. the bulk solution concentration MINUS the Barber-Cushman depletion the diffusion limb has already charged, and with NO MIN against S_mf + S_diff.
 rec 169 WHY: at mode 0 the "ceiling" S_hats = MIN(S_hats_raw, S_mf + S_diff) BINDS ON 7499 OF 7499 ACTIVE DECK-DAYS across all 42 decks, so it is not a bound but the identity S_hats = S_mf + S_diff, and the day's raw zinc supply is EXACTLY 2 x (mass flow + diffusion) -- a factor of two dressed as a transporter. It doubles the level (model +22.73 mg kg-1 above Carducci et al. 2025's printed wheat grain-Zn regression where the observations sit +10.59, 20 decks) and it makes zinc's eCO2, water and nitrogen responses a scaled copy of the mass-flow response, so zinc cannot differ from iron -- and it does not (at most 5 pp apart in all six Braunschweig eCO2 cells), which Gojon et al. 2022 Trends Plant Sci 27:882 DOI 10.1016/j.tplants.2022.04.007 p.2 rules out as a mechanism.
 rec 169 THIS IS A DECLARED CONSTRUCTION, NOT A MEASUREMENT: no Michaelis-Menten zinc influx kinetic for FIELD-grown wheat per unit root mass or root surface area exists on disk or, within the information available to this module, in print. The SHAPE (a high-affinity transporter half-saturated at 2.3 nM) is taken from Hacisalihoglu, Hart & Kochian 2001 Plant Physiol 125:456 DOI 10.1104/pp.125.1.456 Table II p.459 (high-affinity row, apparent Km 2.3 +- 1.0 nM for (-)Zn-grown cv BDME-10; the paper's printed range is 0.6-2.3 nM), which is a 21-d-old HYDROPONIC SEEDLING parameter and whose companion Vmax was found inconsistent with the model's own earlier test runs (grain Zn 50-80x too high). The scale is mm_field_rate(Zn) = 2.36e-3 mg Zn gDW-1 d-1, the EXISTING driver_minerals.csv column-15 value derived from Liu, Liu, Zhang, Chen & Zou 2019 Front Plant Sci 10:426 DOI 10.3389/fpls.2019.00426 -- Table 6 p.8 shoot Zn at maturity 259 g ha-1 + Table 4 p.6 root Zn 16.1 g ha-1 = 27.51 mg m-2, / Table 3 p.6 RDW 483 kg ha-1 = 48.3 g m-2, / a 241-d season (p.3, sown Oct 10/11, harvested Jun 8/10). Neither number is fitted to any campaign observation and NO NEW NUMERAL IS INTRODUCED.
 rec 169 GUARD: IF c_surf <= 0 THE ACTIVE TERM IS 0.0 EXACTLY -- a root surface at or below zero available concentration supports no influx. Where the water-equivalent diffusive flux density q_diff = RLD_e x De_e x mm_depth_m x 86400 x 1e3 is <= 0 (no root, zero effective diffusion coefficient, or a soil water content at which the impedance factor is zero) NO diffusive depletion has been charged, so c_surf falls back to the bulk solution concentration; that is a well-posedness guard against a division by zero, not a second law. Both day counts are printed in the season summary.
 rec 169 NOT CHANGED: Fe, Cu, Mn, Mg and Ca are untouched; the mass-flow, diffusion, phytosiderophore and retired limbs, the pool cap, the organ allocation, the remobilization route and the export fractions are untouched; records 131 and 140 are untouched; the nitrogen chain's own record-139 supply law is NOT touched (this record lives inside mineral_module.f90 only, which keeps its MG0 isolation and writes no C, N, water or energy state). INERT unless rec 131 mineral_supply_law = 1 and rec 140 mineral_supply_mech >= 1 put the zinc limb on the path.
 rec 169 NOT REPAIRED, DISCLOSED: avail_A(Zn) is NOT re-centered by this patch, so the Braunschweig zinc LEVEL on BR102/BR114 is expected to move off its calibration until the lead re-centers it as an INPUT change; the zinc remobilization share (model 26-34 % against Waters, Uauy, Dubcovsky & Grusak 2009 J Exp Bot 60:4263 p.4267 Table 2's 42.6 %) is owned by repair R5b, not by this record; and Mn and Cu still have no active uptake term of any kind.
 rec 171 mineral_n_coupling_basis = 1 : the grain's PHLOEM SINK CAPACITY for a phloem-mobile mineral is set by the grain's PROTEIN (nitrogen), at the per-element grain element:N stoichiometry r_e = driver_minerals.csv column 20 grain_eN_mg_gN [mg element per g grain N].  1 = FLUX (daily) basis, the design note's R5 leg A wording: the day's grain loading <= r_e x MAX(0, dN_grain today).  2 = POOL (cumulative) basis, Xia's own wording: the grain's accumulated content <= r_e x N_grain today.  Refused loading is RETURNED TO ITS SOURCE (uptake share -> leaf terminus, senescence share -> dead tissue), exactly as record 126 already does, so the per-element daily mass balance is unchanged.
 rec 171 SOURCE: Xia, Wang, Qiao, Kong, Xue, Wang, Kong, Xue & Sizmur 2020, Food and Energy Security 9:e243, DOI 10.1002/fes3.243, printed p.7 of 22: "Analysis of the speciation and localization of Zn in wheat grains indicates that Zn interacts with proteins, and therefore, grain protein content (as a physiological sink for Zn) may determine the sink capacity"; printed pp.6-7 for the SHAPE: "zero or relatively low N supply results in low wheat grain Zn concentration, whereas optimal N supply achieves high grain Zn concentration, but excess N supply does not further increase grain Zn, grain N, or protein concentrations"; printed p.7 for the three steps N acts on.  Corroborated first hand by Cakmak 2008 Plant Soil 302:1 printed p.6 and by Waters et al. 2009 J Exp Bot 60:4263 pp.4267-4268, already this module's senescence-export basis.
 rec 171 THE CONSTANT IS DECLARED ABSENT: grain_eN_mg_gN ships 0.0 (= no bound) for all six elements, the same convention record 126's grain_max_mg_kg already uses, because NO first-hand wheat-grain primary on disk prints a grain element:N or element:protein stoichiometry (null-safe sweep of both textbook trees; Kutman 2010, Peleg 2008, Fan 2008 and Zhao 2009 are absent). Taking r_e from the campaign's own measured grain would be fitting to the falsification target and is forbidden.  With all six at 0.0 this record is a PROVABLE NO-OP at every mode.
 rec 171 NOT CLAIMED: nitrogen enters as a CEILING only, so the N-driven INCREASE in total uptake that Xia p.7 also reports is NOT modeled and the N-dose CONTENT magnitude shortfall is not addressed; root uptake, root-to-shoot transport, the senescence export fractions, the soil impedance pair and the Zn HATS bound are untouched (other repairs, other records); and because grain protein FALLS under eCO2 a binding ceiling makes the eCO2 CONTENT response slightly MORE negative -- this record and the eCO2 magnitude shortfall pull in opposite directions.
 rec 171 ISOLATION: N_storage and N_chaff enter mineral_module.f90 READ-ONLY (N_grain = MAX(0, N_storage - N_chaff), the SAME expression main_MMCO2Crop.f90 already uses for grainN_conc_b3 and grain_protein_pct) and appear on no left-hand side there; nothing is written to the nitrogen chain or the carbon chain, and the module's MG0 isolation is unchanged.
 rec 129 sink_full_carbon_fate = 1 : while the grain sink is full, the rec-92 deposition window is lifted for that surplus (storage continues to the existing wsc_cap_frac capacity); the remainder is booked to an explicit, reported unallocated-assimilate carbon loss (cfo_loss_day/cum), not to respiration and not to stem structure, superseding the rec-127 residual for this surplus. No wheat overflow-respiration rate law exists in the library on disk, and photosynthetic down-regulation by a full sink is not supported in wheat (Schnyder 1993 p.238); neither is modeled. SHARED.
 rec 175 grain_n_partition_basis = 4 : mode 1 corrects an earlier formulation.  Record 158's own header declares that ndb_rate_prev is "continuous across anthesis"; record 154 sets N_from_assim_day = 0 by construction, the three N_alloc_* terms are already zeroed post-anthesis, so the sum is IDENTICALLY ZERO after anthesis, N_max = MIN(1.21, 0) = 0 and the shoot stops reducing nitrate the day after anthesis.
 rec 175 MODE 1: the sum gains the record-154 limb's OWN de novo reduction demand on the day -- grain import + lamina + stem + chaff synthesis, every term already computed and already printed in output/daily_organ_n_turnover.csv.  Busch, Sage & Farquhar 2018 Nature Plants 4:46-54 (DOI 10.1038/s41477-017-0065-x) p.49 limiter (b), the DEMAND, which is the limiter record 158 mode 1 elected.  ZERO NEW CONSTANTS; the Busch ceiling N_max = 1.21 umol m-2 s-1 (printed in the Fig. 3a parameter block p.52) stays outermost.
 rec 175 MODE 2: the model applies FPB Eqn 12's (p.785) RATE and discards its INITIAL CONDITION.  Bertheloot, Andrieu, Fournier & Martre 2008 Funct Plant Biol 35:781-796 (DOI 10.1071/FP08064) p.786 verbatim: "grain N mass at anthesis, N_g^tot(0), was set at 2.4 mg (Girard 1997)", Table 1 p.784 "N_g^tot(0) ... kg ... 2.4 x 10^-6" -- the number the model ALREADY carries as gnf_ng0_per_ear and ALREADY uses to seed the potential.  Mode 2 charges the deficit to the spike's own N inside the ear (N_chaff down, N_storage unchanged), down to the chaff structural floor; a refused draw is COUNTED and PRINTED, never silent.  ZERO NEW CONSTANTS.
 rec 175 MODE 3: the grain's UNMET sink joins the synthesis limbs' pro-rata claim set (Bertheloot 2011a p.1090; Bertheloot 2011a Eqn 12 p.1091 = FPB Eqn 6 p.784; sigma 1.5e-4/3.0e-5, p_r 0.1, delta 0.008, k1 0.0018, k2 864000, all Bertheloot 2011b Table 2 p.1101 and all already in the code).  PRE-REGISTERED AS INERT: the grain is served FIRST from the pool, so on a short day the pool is exactly 0 when the limbs resolve and on a served day the residual is 0.  A mode-3 run must be BYTE-IDENTICAL to a mode-2 run; if it is not, the prediction is falsified and is reported.
 rec 175 MODE 4: the Ngtot(0) HANDOVER is paid against the GRAIN'S OWN DRY MASS, not as a lump on a grain of zero mass.  Mode 2 relabels gnf_ng0 (1.550 g N m-2 at WDF25_Ruta_aCO2_WW) from chaff to grain on the first fill day, on which W_grain = 0.00 g m-2, so the grain's N concentration on that day is unbounded.  FPB 2008 p.786/Table 1 p.784 print Ngtot(0) = 2.4 mg with NO dry-mass clause, so mode 2 is NOT repaired in place.  Bertheloot, Wu, Cournede & Andrieu 2011 Ann Bot 108:1097-1109 Table 1(a) 'Grains' (DOI 10.1093/aob/mcr125) publishes the SAME initial condition PAIRED with a dry mass: 'Total N mass N_grain^tot mg 2.4' and 'Total dry mass M_grain^tot mg 120', i.e. 0.020 g N g-1 DM = 2.0 % DM.  Mode 4 therefore charges MIN(gnf_ng0, 0.020 x W_grain) cumulatively, the chaff structural floor still refusing what it cannot pay.  ONE constant, a measured quotient of two cells of one table.
 rec 148 wsc_fate_law = 1 : 1 = the law (term A + term B), 2 = term A only, 3 = term B only. Term A restores the rec-92 DEPOSITION CLOSE for the grain-sink-full surplus (Schnyder 1993 New Phytol 123:233 p.238, WSC accumulate "until 10-20 d after anthesis"; p.233 Summary, "terminates within three weeks following anthesis"), the refused carbon travelling the existing rec-127/129 overflow path to cfo_loss_day/cum; the rec-129 window LIFT and its withdrawn justification are superseded (misquote corrected at SHARED). Term B opens the rec-105 = 2 release at TERMINAL GRAIN-SINK CLOSURE (gfb_end_bound /= 0; Schnyder 1993 p.240, grain sink capacity "fixed at 2-3 wk after anthesis and ... sink-limited thereafter") and spreads the standing pool to maturity entirely to cres_respired at unity (p.240, whole-plant respiration rises while the stem WSC is lost), the grain never fed (room = 0 at and after that gate, so gain2 = 0 by the existing arithmetic). Zero new numeric constants. SHARED.
 rec 130 grain_n_min_conc = 3 : grain DM filling is capped so cumulative grain N never implies a concentration below 1.5% (Sinclair & Amir 1992, via Jamieson & Semenov 2000 FCR 68:21 p.23-24, "grain growth can be limited directly by lack of N"); 1 = cumulative room = N_grain/0.015 - W_grain; 2 = guarded daily increment dW_grain <= dN_grain(t-1)/0.015, not evaluated below 10% of the rec-118 potential kernel mass. A THIRD ceiling alongside rec 118 / rec 125 (MIN of all active ceilings' room); the refused DM flows into the existing rec 127/129 fate chain unchanged. SHARED.
 rec 131 mineral_supply_law = 1 : Fe/Zn/Cu/Mn soil-solution concentration + a generalized per-root-mass active term are driven by ONE calibrated site-level availability parameter each (driver_minerals.csv column 17 avail_A_mgL_CAL); Ca xylem concentration driven by ONE calibrated parameter (column 18 xylem_Ca_mgL_CAL), replacing the borrowed 54.9 mg/L analogue-soil ceiling; the Lizana 2010 grain-water import ratio (0.7625 g H2O g-1 final grain DM) stays measured, unchanged. Mg untouched. SHARED/mineral_module.f90.
 rec 140 mineral_supply_mech = 1 : rec 131's calibrated generalized active term is RETIRED for Fe/Zn/Cu/Mn; mass flow (unchanged) + diffusion to the root surface (Barber-Cushman, reusing rec 139's own RLD/SRL and the SAME declared f_l(theta) pair) + (Zn only) a bounded HATS ceiling (Hacisalihoglu 2001 Table II, capped at S_mf+S_diff, never a field rate) now carry Fe/Zn/Cu/Mg/Mn uptake; Ca xylem route unchanged. SHARED/mineral_module.f90.
 rec 99 tiller_survival_mech = 4 : tiller carbon affordability, deaths capped day by day by Abichou Eqn T4.4 F(tau_n) (theta 3.32, delta 1.77) x U(t), the cull target F(tau_n)*U locked by the monotone MAX; endpoint at flag-leaf ligulation. SHARED.
 rec 89 grain_number_mech = 1 (A+D): Fischer 1985 spike window + 0.44 partition; grain number PREDICTED per axis (100 florets g-1, 0.78 kernels per floret). FE, storage_onset_dvs2 and storage_peak_frac are NOT READ.
 rec 90 floret_survival_mech = 4: floret-site chain; ear-bearing by SPIKE AFFORDABILITY phi_sp = MIN(1, W_axis / (bgn_r_spike x window degCd)) per class, continuous, no bar; earless axes standing (Fischer 1985 p.452); pool returned to ear-bearers. SHARED.
 rec 91 grain_fill_mech = 1: kernel growth RATE x filling DURATION. Yin 2003 Ann Bot 91:361 Tab 2 beta rate (c_m 1.9283 mg kernel-1 d-1 at 17.5 C, +0.11067 per K, t_m/t_e 0.4331); duration 405.581 degCd above 6.6187 C, DERIVED from that table by Fischer 1985 Tab 6 p.455. TKW_potential is NOT READ.
 rec 92 stem_wsc_mech = 1: stem WSC gets a CAPACITY (0.50 of stem DM), net deposition ENDS 15 d after anthesis, and remobilisation is DEMAND-DRIVEN (Schnyder 1993 New Phytol 123:233 pp.233/238/239). reserve_remob_rate is NOT READ.
   NOTE: overflow_to_reserve_total now reports the surplus LABELLED as WSC, not the surplus moved to the stem. No carbon moves either way.
 rec 105 wsc_reserve_law = 2 (rec 107 release-window member 2) : THE REPAIR -- the stem WSC pool is RELEASED over the window REGARDLESS of the grain deficit (rel = MIN(W_reserve, W_stem, cap), cap = W_reserve x dtau/tau_rem), and the deficit decides ONLY the grain share: CASE 1 rel_g = MIN(rel, room/eff) -> grain at the rec 60 Gebbing efficiency; CASE 2 rel_f = rel - rel_g -> the NAMED ledger cres_respired AT UNITY (no efficiency). Members: 1 = item-B filling clock (gfb_dfill - gfb_tt) / 2 = legacy rec-59 clock (reserve_end_dvs2 - dvs2); SWEPT, never collapsed. rec 106 NOT READ. rec 100 = 0 legal. SHARED. Off by default.
 rec 118 kernel_mass_ceiling = 1 : per-kernel mass bounded by the MEASURED cultivar TKW_potential =    31.0000     g per 1000 kernels (input/cultivar_yield.csv row 2), inside the rec-91 rate x duration law (Yin et al. 2003 Ann Bot 91:361 Table 2 w_max; Sofield et al. 1977 Aust J Plant Physiol 4:785).  SHARED.f90.  v1.0.0 fix A, approved 2026-10-05.
 rec 94 canopy_n_flag_zone = 3: THE ITEM. Mode 1 plus the layered f_PAR of FPB Eqn 17 p.785 inside item F's Eqn-6 limb (audit note (iii)).
 rec 86 grainN_sink_mech = 1: THE ITEM. Grain N = min(potential per-ear sink, available N) -- Bertheloot, Martre & Andrieu 2008 FPB 35:781 Eqn 11-12 p.785, Table 1 p.784 (N_g(0) = 2.4 mg ear-1, g = 0.005 degCd-1 DECLARED DERIVED NOT MEASURED, tau = 250 degCd, thermal time base 0 C). Supply = assimilation + mobile pool + delta-limited organ draw above the p.1711 structural floors. Post-anthesis UPTAKE demand read off the SAME potential (the Jamieson & Semenov NHI trajectory is retired). Critical-N shoot mass on W_grain+W_chaff.
   EQN-6 REPAIR 2026-09-21: lamina photosynthetic N now runs FPB Eqn 4 in FULL -- Eqn 5 degradation (delta = 0.008 [degCd]-1) AND Eqn 6 synthesis (sigma = 0.0015 [degCd]-1, k1 = 0.0018 kg kg-1, k2 = 10 J m-2 s-1, all FPB Table 1 p.784), on the Eqn-1 p.783 pool basis N^ph = (N^tot - N^struct)/(1+r) with r = 0.10 (p.786). FPB p.786 fitted sigma, delta, k1 and k2 JOINTLY across Eqns 5 AND 6, so delta is only sourced when sigma is present.
